From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SableOS <noreply@sableos.invalid>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 13:29:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] SableOS: Phone follows the system Dark theme

Phone now looks like every other Sable app: light while the system Dark
theme is off, dark while it is on, instead of dark whatever the setting.

* sable_colors.xml holds a light Sable palette (light surfaces, dark text,
  system_accent1_600 accent on a system_accent1_100 container); the dark
  palette from 0707 moves unchanged to values-night. Every 0707/0708
  resource already points at these tokens, so rows, the search pill, the
  dial pad, pills and the focus outline follow without further change.
* The Dialer base and alert dialog themes inherit the AppCompat DayNight
  themes, the action bar overlays are DayNight, the status and navigation
  bar icons are dark on the light palette (sable_light_bars) and bottom
  sheets use the light or dark design sheet (SableBottomSheetDialog).
* The call screen stays dark, as upstream (its text is white on the call
  background): InCallActivity resolves its resources as in the Dark theme.
* The disabled voicemail icon tint uses the disabled text token.

No behaviour change.
